WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.533 --> 00:00:16.414
Nancy put all her energy into scrubbing and sweeping the little attic room.

2
00:00:18.155 --> 00:00:22.477
Remembering Miss Polly's instructions, she made sure the corners were especially clean.

3
00:00:22.497 --> 00:00:29.240
"I wish I could clean out the corners of Miss Polly's heart," Nancy said as she swept up

4
00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:30.000
a cloud of dust.

5
00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:36.061
Nancy was afraid of Miss Polly, but she also had plenty of opinions about her employer.

6
00:00:39.302 --> 00:00:45.024
"The idea of sticking that poor child way up here in this hot, tiny room!"

7
00:00:45.824 --> 00:00:47.765
Nancy stopped to wipe some sweat from her face.

8
00:00:47.785 --> 00:00:54.246
"In summer it's uncomfortable, and in winter there won't be any fireplace to warm her.

9
00:00:55.487 --> 00:00:59.188
With all the nice rooms in this house, Miss Polly picked this one?

10
00:01:00.264 --> 00:01:06.790
Unbelievable!" For a while Nancy worked in silence.

11
00:01:08.371 --> 00:01:10.313
Then she looked around the room in disgust.

12
00:01:11.614 --> 00:01:16.458
There were no pictures or colorful curtains; there was nothing to make the space bright or cheerful.

13
00:01:16.478 --> 00:01:19.100
"Well, my part's done."

14
00:01:20.261 --> 00:01:22.943
Nancy wrung out a wet rag until her fingers ached.

15
00:01:22.963 --> 00:01:28.428
"There's no dirt here—or anything else.

16
00:01:29.336 --> 00:01:32.879
What a terrible place to put a homesick, lonely child!"

17
00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:36.321
Nancy left the room and slammed the door.

18
00:01:36.341 --> 00:01:39.743
"Oops!" Nancy bit her lip in fear.

19
00:01:40.944 --> 00:01:43.646
Then she stood up tall and said, "I don't care!

20
00:01:43.666 --> 00:01:46.708
I hope Miss Polly heard that and was annoyed!"

21
00:01:50.311 --> 00:01:53.833
Nancy went into the backyard, where Tom, the gardener, was pulling weeds.

22
00:01:54.894 --> 00:01:57.856
She looked quickly over her shoulder to be sure Miss Polly wasn't watching.

23
00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:02.182
"Tom, did you know a child is coming to live here?"

24
00:02:02.202 --> 00:02:05.524
"Coming to live with Miss Polly?"

25
00:02:06.665 --> 00:02:08.646
The old man straightened up with difficulty.

26
00:02:08.666 --> 00:02:11.207
"You must be joking."

27
00:02:11.227 --> 00:02:14.269
"Miss Polly told me herself.

28
00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:19.212
It's her niece, Pollyanna, and she's an 11-year-old orphan."

29
00:02:20.913 --> 00:02:21.594
Tom smiled.

30
00:02:21.614 --> 00:02:24.716
"That must be Miss Jennie's girl.

31
00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:29.363
I can't believe these old eyes will actually get to see her."

32
00:02:29.383 --> 00:02:31.585
"Who's Miss Jennie?"

33
00:02:31.905 --> 00:02:32.566
Nancy asked.

34
00:02:32.586 --> 00:02:38.550
"She was Miss Polly's sister, and she was wonderful," Tom said.

35
00:02:38.571 --> 00:02:41.233
"Such a kind person.

36
00:02:42.233 --> 00:02:45.816
Miss Jennie left here to marry a minister a long time ago.

37
00:02:47.037 --> 00:02:49.019
Last we heard she'd died."

38
00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:55.124
"Well, Miss Polly is making Pollyanna sleep in the attic."

39
00:02:56.500 --> 00:03:00.203
Nancy glanced over her shoulder again to be sure Miss Polly wasn't nearby.

40
00:03:00.223 --> 00:03:03.565
"Miss Polly should be ashamed of herself!"

41
00:03:05.186 --> 00:03:07.648
Tom went back to pulling weeds but started chuckling.

42
00:03:10.950 --> 00:03:11.791
"What's so funny?"

43
00:03:12.151 --> 00:03:14.072
Nancy asked, squatting next to him.

44
00:03:14.092 --> 00:03:19.096
"I wonder what Miss Polly will do with a child in the house."

45
00:03:19.116 --> 00:03:24.900
"Humph! I wonder what a child will do with Miss Polly in the house."

46
00:03:26.212 --> 00:03:27.753
Now Tom was laughing heartily.

47
00:03:33.036 --> 00:03:35.397
obvious you're not fond of Miss Polly."

48
00:03:35.417 --> 00:03:39.559
"As if anybody could be fond of her!"

49
00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:44.162
Nancy yanked out a weed and tossed it into Tom's wheelbarrow.

50
00:03:45.343 --> 00:03:46.503
Tom raised his eyebrows.

51
00:03:46.523 --> 00:03:50.946
"I guess you don't know about Miss Polly's broken engagement."

52
00:03:52.386 --> 00:03:53.727
"Broken engagement?

53
00:03:54.648 --> 00:03:56.981
Her?" Tom nodded.

54
00:03:57.001 --> 00:04:00.744
"The fellow still lives right here in town."

55
00:04:00.764 --> 00:04:03.246
"Who is it?"

56
00:04:03.967 --> 00:04:05.408
Nancy looked at him eagerly.

57
00:04:06.669 --> 00:04:08.711
Tom put a hand on his aching back and stood up.

58
00:04:09.431 --> 00:04:11.353
"No, no, I can't tell you.

59
00:04:11.373 --> 00:04:14.856
It's not right that I reveal Miss Polly's secret."

60
00:04:14.876 --> 00:04:18.158
"It just doesn't seem possible."

61
00:04:18.179 --> 00:04:26.433
"Think of it like a mystery in one of those books you're always reading," Tom teased her.

62
00:04:27.913 --> 00:04:28.874
Nancy shook her head.

63
00:04:28.894 --> 00:04:33.537
"I still don't believe that anyone could be in love with Miss Polly."

64
00:04:33.557 --> 00:04:40.921
"Years ago Miss Polly was quite pretty, and she would be now Tom hesitated.

65
00:04:40.941 --> 00:04:42.942
"If she let herself."

66
00:04:44.763 --> 00:04:46.844
"Pretty? Miss Polly?"

67
00:04:46.864 --> 00:04:52.628
"Yes, she didn't always pull her hair back so tight.

68
00:04:53.716 --> 00:04:58.198
She used to wear flowers on her bonnets and lace trim on her dresses.

69
00:04:59.438 --> 00:05:03.320
If she did all that again, you'd see she's not so old."

70
00:05:03.340 --> 00:05:08.742
"Well, she does a good imitation of a cranky old person.

71
00:05:09.803 --> 00:05:11.263
There's no pleasing her now."

72
00:05:13.564 --> 00:05:14.965
"That's certainly true.

73
00:05:16.185 --> 00:05:19.326
It all started with that argument with her sweetheart."

74
00:05:21.127 --> 00:05:23.765
"She shouldn't take it out on us," Nancy said.

75
00:05:23.785 --> 00:05:27.508
"If my family didn't need the money, I'd quit.

76
00:05:29.049 --> 00:05:33.213
One day I'll get so mad that I'll say something I shouldn't, and she'll fire me."

77
00:05:33.233 --> 00:05:37.396
"Nancy!" a sharp voice called from a window.

78
00:05:39.178 --> 00:05:42.340
Nancy's eyes widened in fear, and she dashed for the house.

79
00:05:44.082 --> 00:05:44.743
"Yes, ma'am!

80
00:05:45.043 --> 00:05:45.904
I'm coming, ma'am!"
